{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/229433-using-trinity-for-a-40k-rpg","id":229433,"title":"Using Trinity for a 40K RPG","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-15T12:38:37-07:00","id":229433,"title":"Using Trinity for a 40K RPG","content":"Disclaimer: Apologies if this is the wrong forum for this topic.<br /> <br /> I am a huge, huge fan of Warhammer 40,000, and I have been ever since the first edition of the game. As you can imagine, I was really interested when Games Workshop and later, Fantasy Flight Games started making role playing games based on the setting. However, I have to say, percentile dice systems do not seem to agree with me. In The first game of Dark heresy I ran, what was intended to be a dramatic, climactic duel resulted in both combatants flailing comically at each other for several turns, unable to hit anything. Perhaps I just need more experiance with the rules, or to house rule them a bit, but I can't help thinking that I'd rather just port the game over to the storyteller system, which I am much more familier with.<br /> I've been considering this for a couple of weeks now, and I think that Trinity could do a fairly good job of emulating Dark Heresy. Psions are not a perfect fit for Sanctioned Psykers, but I think they are close enough, with some notable exceptions. The various non-powered types of character would be simple to represent. I would have to do a fair bit of homebrewing, especially for certain weapons, but I think that it would be worthwhile. <br /> I would welcome any constructive suggestions that people might have on the matter, especially if they have tried something similar themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T13:22:09-07:00","id":230470,"title":"","content":"Here are some ideas that I've had so far;<br /> <br /> The Auto, shotgun, laser and web weapons in the Trinity main rulebook as well as plasma pistols from the Technology manual = their 40k counterparts<br /> <br /> Flechette weapons = Dark Eldar Splinter weapons<br /> <br /> Coil Carbines from the Technology Manual = Bolt guns.<br /> <br /> Clairsentience, Psychokinesis, Telepathy and Vitakinesis are all available as Apitudes for imperial Psykers. Biokinesis does not seem appropriate, at least not for human psykers. Quantakinesis and Teleportation I'm undecided about.<br /> <br /> Electrokinesis I intend to re-skin to represent Adeptus Mechanicus Implants. Just substitute &quot;Psi&quot; for &quot;Tech&quot; or &quot;Blessing of the Machine God&quot; or some similar fitting term. It may not be an exact match, but I think it's close enough.<br /> <br /> The Cyberware rules in Asia Ascendant should work well for other bionics. Just remove the restrictions on Backing.<br /> <br /> VARGs stand in fairly well for Dreadnoughts, Tau Battlesuits, and similar walkers. Just need a few alterations, and they should work fine. The Technology Manual has rules for making custom vehicles, so that should be very helpful in creating other vehicles.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T18:04:24-07:00","id":235998,"title":"","content":"maybe VARS for powerarmour. (it is in the core rule book) may want to upgrade for space marines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T10:54:08-07:00","id":236668,"title":"","content":"That's a good idea. For actual space marines, I might hold off for a bit until I get the basics worked out. I have some ideas, but they involve borrowing some rules from other game lines (Such as Mega Strength from Aberrant) and are in no way balanced with default characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}